25.theory:
## submit

Form submission event:

```js
const form = document.querySelector("form");
form.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
  event.preventDefault();
  console.log("submission intercepted");
});
```

By default submit **reloads** the page. `preventDefault()` cancels the default behavior.

## preventDefault

```js
event.preventDefault();
```

Stops the default action. For clicks — link navigation, for forms — submission.

## Field value

```js
const input = document.querySelector("#name");
const value = input.value;
```

`value` — what is typed.

## Example

```js
form.addEventListener("submit", (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const text = input.value;
  output.textContent = text;
});
```

## reset

```js
form.reset();  // clear fields
input.value = "";  // clear one
```

## input

`input` event — on each change:

```js
input.addEventListener("input", () => {
  console.log(input.value);
});
```

## What if

- Forget `preventDefault` — page reloads, JS won't finish.
- `e.preventDefault` without `()` — not called.

## Common mistake

`submit` without `preventDefault` — reload. Always prevent.

## Summary

- `submit` — on form
- `preventDefault()` — cancel
- `input.value` — value
- `form.reset()` — clear
- `input` — on each change

26.theory:
## keydown

```js
document.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
  console.log(event.key);
});
```

Fires on key press.

## event.key

`event.key` — character or name:

- `"a"` — letter
- `"Enter"` — Enter
- `"Escape"` — Esc
- `"ArrowUp"` / `"ArrowDown"` — arrows
- `" "` — space

## Other properties

- `event.code` — physical code (`"KeyA"`, `"Space"`)
- `event.ctrlKey` / `shiftKey` / `altKey` — modifiers (true/false)

```js
document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
  if (e.ctrlKey && e.key === "s") {
    e.preventDefault();
    console.log("save intercepted");
  }
});
```

## keyup

```js
document.addEventListener("keyup", (e) => {
  console.log("released", e.key);
});
```

Fires on release.

## What if

- `event.key` for dead keys (Shift) — `"Shift"`.
- `preventDefault` on all keydown — breaks Tab, arrows.

## Common mistake

`event.keyCode` — legacy. Use `event.key`.

## Summary

- `keydown` — press
- `event.key` — character or name
- `ctrlKey` / `shiftKey` — modifiers
- `keyCode` — legacy

27.theory:
## What we build

Counter with + and − buttons. Uses: DOM, events, text update.

## HTML

```html
<button id="dec">−</button>
<span id="value">0</span>
<button id="inc">+</button>
```

## JS

```js
let count = 0;
const value = document.querySelector("#value");
const inc = document.querySelector("#inc");
const dec = document.querySelector("#dec");

inc.addEventListener("click", () => {
  count++;
  value.textContent = count;
});

dec.addEventListener("click", () => {
  count--;
  value.textContent = count;
});
```

## Checks

- `count` — variable holding current
- `textContent` — updated
- `addEventListener` on two buttons
- `++` / `--`

## What if

- `value.textContent = count++` — shows old, then ++.
- Forget `textContent` update — number doesn't change.

## Common mistake

`count = value.textContent + 1` — string concat. Use `Number(...)` or keep `count` numeric.

## Summary

- `let count` — state
- `addEventListener` on buttons
- `textContent` — update
- `count++` / `count--`

